    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d767">

                <pb facs="0619" n="503" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg503"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/23452c.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                            Special Commissioners.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-05-21">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 21, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>In view of the commanding position the Constitutionalists have secured in Mexico
                    and the necessity of considering the views of those whom they represent, the
                    President suggests that you ask the Mediators whether they do not consider it
                    advisable to renew the invitation to the Constitutionalists to send
                    commissioners without attempting to define the scope of what is to be discussed
                    and without reference to <pb facs="0620" n="504" xml:id="pg504"/> the suspension
                    of hostilities. It is likely to involve many delays and uncertainties if the
                    discussion is conducted without them, and it is extremely difficult to confer
                    with them satisfactorily by indirect ways such as are open to us here.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bryan</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
